  "question": {
    "text": "A particle is moving in a circle of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;under the action of a force <math><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><msup><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> which is directed towards centre of the circle. Total mechanical energy (kinetic energy + potential energy) of the particle is (take potential energy<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>):",
    "image": null
  },
